"That January month was very busy," mother said.
I agreed to that.
"Everything changed very fast," I told mother.
In January, everything was new.
In the beginning, I felt a little fear.
But, this city quickly became familiar to me.
I got good friends here.
Last week, I did not feel that old fear.
Yesterday when I sat in the room, I felt great peace.
Because of all this, Kochi is now like my own home.
"You are happy there," mother said with a smile.
"Yes, I am very happy here," I replied.
On the screen, Lola moved slowly.
She was in a deep sleep.
We talked for some more time.
After the call, I looked into my room.
I liked my life in Kochi.
That thought gave me great happiness.
